{'name': 'Minnow Cafe', 'address': '9 Breakwater', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Delis', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-11 16:25:16', 'review_text': 'This place is perfect to get some seafood in Santa Barbara! I was glad to be able to find this hole in a wall while walking with my group for lunch. 

I ordered the clam chowder bread bowl and fish and chips. Clam chowder was very delicious and fresh. The fish was crispy and made into perfection. 

The best part is that you can order the food right away and simply sit at the tables outside to eat near the harbor where the ocean is so close. So if you want to get food in a quickly manner in order to have more time to explore the other areas in Santa Barbara, I would highly recommend Minnow Cafe.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-04-08 00:39:53', 'review_text': 'Hard to beat for a fast-food-type breakfast or lunch at the marina. Simple, good food, well prepared.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2011-03-20 03:51:33', 'review_text': "I really like the Minnow...I mean you can't beat the location for a fast food establishment and the Fish Tacos are pretty good...BUT I'm always horrified to discover how much this fast food experience costs.  I mean, it's really not very good food unless you view it as cheap (but it's not).  Great thing, sitting outside by the harbor watching the BPs go by while you eat cheap (seeming) food.  Bad part, greasy spoon food served on paper plates by snarky staff with condiments that blow away...but it ain't cheap.  Guess that's Santa Barbara."}]}

{'name': "TonyRay's Restaurant & Cantina", 'address': '731 De La Guerra Plz', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Nightlife, Restaurants, Mexican, Dance Clubs', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2014-04-14 16:30:03', 'review_text': "Been to Tony Ray's for the occasional party.   DJ Fab or bunch of drunk Harley dudes, certainly a Fiesta or two.  

As many times as I have been there, I don't really know what it is?   Is it a restaurant?  Does it keep regular hours?   Is it a bar?  Do people go there and hang out on a Thursday night?   The bartenders have always been nice and the drinks have been good.  Not sure if they have glass because it seems that I am always served in a plastic cup.   I know I have eaten the food but I have zero recollection as to whether or not I enjoyed it, it is that forgettable.  

I gave them two stars but I might go back and see if they deserve and upgrade."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2014-03-02 15:38:33', 'review_text': "This is a great spot for a drink and some dessert. The dinner menu is decent but the price and size do not match. Don't come hungry, but do enjoy a specialty drink."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-29 21:40:05', 'review_text': 'my daughters and friends love to go there for karaoke :) so fun! The owners and staff are very sweet!'}]}

{'name': 'Blenders In the Grass', 'address': '1046 Coast Village Rd, Ste F', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Juice Bars & Smoothies, Food, Restaurants, Vegetarian', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-22:0', 'Friday': '7:0-18:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': None, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-09 04:23:38', 'review_text': 'I went to blenders and ordered 2 drinks.  One was a blue pomegranate and it was made short even after using the spatula to pour any excess smoothie into the cup. I know the smoothie is supposed to reach the top of the cup because I used to be a supervisor there. This is not the first time this has happened, it seems to be a reoccurring problem.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-09-21 16:07:13', 'review_text': 'The blenders in montecito last night I go to the register the girl working it goes to it too and just blankly stares at me.

No hello what can I get you no acknowledgment or greeting. I have to initiate my order.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-05-17 20:01:12', 'review_text': 'If you like added sugar in their ice milk and sherbet and non organic gmo tasting fruit and soy milk then this is your place! The fruit juice they add tastes like corn syrup and sugar, maybe 10% real juice.
I dont even think their wheat grass is organic as nothing is labeled organic and non gmo. Hit or miss on customer service and sanitary procedures as it looks as the college kids working their are trying to make them as fast as they can and rarely even blend them long enough, I was loyal but the last straw was when I bought a peanut butter bar and it tasted like moldy peanuts as I looked at the expiration date, it was 3 months expired! The owners have lost touch and the managers are not into customer service. So long...'}]}

{'name': 'Haggen Food & Pharmacy', 'address': '175 N Fairview Ave', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Delis, Drugstores, Restaurants, Food, Shopping, Grocery, Bakeries', 'hours': {'Monday': '6:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '6:0-0:0', 'Thursday': '6:0-0:0', 'Friday': '6:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '6:0-0:0', 'Sunday': '6:0-0:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 2.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2015-11-02 06:05:33', 'review_text': "Went in after the change from Vons for some whole wheat flour and was surprised that the flour was over $8 for 5 pounds. Next time I went to Smart and final and the King Arthur flour is $3.99 regular price. I live in Goleta so next time I went back to Haggens to compare and they had the King Arthur flour for $6.49 with 20% off which is still $5.15. I have been shopping in the same store since the Safeway opened in the 60's but I am done now with this kind of price increase."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2015-10-26 10:12:53', 'review_text': 'I decided to give this Haggen location a chance. I walked into an mostly empty store. I notice some items that have been marked down in the deli due to product expiring the same day. I take it up to the register. The store manager was at the register. She refused to honor the discount on the packaging and said it was a mistake. Haggen, you can keep your expired food!'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2015-10-22 07:50:28', 'review_text': 'Really? I know you're going out of business Haggen but you expect me to pack my own groceries now? 

Now, even though I am an educated professional on a 6+ figure salary, I am not above stuffing some groceries in a shopping bag. It's obviously not difficult. However, if you want me to do your job for you, you've got to be nice to me. Last time I was in the store the portly middle aged man just threw my groceries onto the conveyer belt and left them to pile up at the end. He never acknowledged my existence except to grunt the total to me. 

You can either pack my damn groceries or I walk out next time. Not sorry you'll soon be out of a job if that's the level of "service" you provide. Pfft.'}]}

{'name': 'Oakberry Açaí Bowls and Smoothies', 'address': '819-B State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Coffee & Tea, Restaurants, Cafes, Food, Acai Bowls, Juice Bars & Smoothies', 'hours': {'Monday': '8:0-20:0', 'Tuesday': '8:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '8:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '8:0-18:0', 'Friday': '9:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-20:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-22 19:05:43', 'review_text': "Great Açaí! We stopped here for a quick lunch and it didn't disappoint! Lots of fresh fruit available ans a great variety of toppings. Açaí was a bit thinner than other types I've had but still had great flavor. The chai pudding topping was my favorite - never had that before and it was a nice addition! Would stop by again for sure!"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-19 00:38:41', 'review_text': 'Love this place for a quick lunch or a pick me up! There are plenty of choices for toppings and they have gluten free options. I like adding coconut, peanut butter, bananas, strawberries and granola. My reasoning for the four stars is i feel it is a little overpriced.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-19 03:30:05', 'review_text': '5 star acai bowl, service, and location.  So impressed with this last minute find.  It ended up being a light dinner kinda night for us and with not much open at almost 8pm, but these bowls hit the spot.  

Once you choose the size you want, there is a large list of toppings which are unlimited.  I chose everything that sounded good and I was so impressed with how well they all went together.  My first time having peanut butter with my acai and chai pudding but it messed well.  Fresh, flavorful and filling.  

I know where to stop now when in Santa Barbara.'}]}

{'name': 'De La Vina Lounge', 'address': '2711 De La Vina St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Dive Bars, Bars, Lounges, Nightlife, Pool Halls, Sports Bars', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-2:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-2:0', 'Friday': '10:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': True, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-05-18 05:56:58', 'review_text': 'Alice is a saint! Loved finding this gem in Santa Barbara. Enjoy the family vibes when you enter.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-05-12 05:17:30', 'review_text': 'I really hate updating reviews.   First impressions, right??  But in the case of Jimboz, how could I not. I don't want to call myself a regular because honestly I have never been there at 10am for The Price Is Right and never make it more than once in a week.  But I will say I'm a huge fan!  I usually go on Tuesdays which is officially "Ladies Night".  But Alice is always working and treats me like her bestie!!! Nobody pours a Grand Mariner better than Alice.   What?  They do fancy???   Hell Yes!!  Premium tequilas, good Bourbon, they have it.... but most of all you feel at home, they have very welcoming regulars.   If someone is doing a food run, you will probably be included.   Isn't that what a neighborhood bar should be about??'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-04-15 23:35:01', 'review_text': 'Sometimes YOU "get what YOU pay for" & sometimes YOU get just WHAT you're looking for...!  Especially if it is that "throwback" friendly "tavern" of Ol'!  That The "dufas hipsters" like to refer as a "dive bar", because they have NO reference points in their own generation!

Anyway if YOU are looking for a small, intimate NO FRILLS, friendly lil' place to "toss back a few" w/ your friends and/or solo THIS should be on your "go to LIST"...!!!

Plenty of GOOD restaurants within in walking distance...'}]}

{'name': "Rudy's Mexican Restaurant & Take Out", 'address': '811 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-02-04 13:52:45', 'review_text': 'Oh man, I love the Energy Burrito with chicken here. It's probably the furthest from authentic you can get, but authenticity doesn't have a monopoly on delicious! I like it so much I simply haven't tried the other options, though I hear they're good (and pretty authentic). 

I would say the consistency isn't the best - sometimes it's a bland or weirdly dry or otherwise "off," but when they do it right it's my second favorite burrito. Love to let the juice from the burrito run onto the tortilla chips that come with...'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-11 18:14:18', 'review_text': "I would go here again but I would stick with a simple chicken taco and nothing that sounds greasy.  The shrimp quesadilla was just too much cheese and greasy.  If that's what you're into then you'll love it.  Probably not the best food choice if you're at all health conscious.  But if you order smart you'll be just fine.  The food is good.  The salsa bar is exceptional.  Fresh everything to suit anyone's needs for whatever plate you order.  You can order a Mexican beer here to go with your meal which is always a plus.  I would recommend, but watch what you order."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2011-09-04 00:10:38', 'review_text': "Energy burrito - whole wheat tortilla, grilled chicken, jack cheese & romaine lettuce. 

Honestly, the burrito was only okay. If it were for the guacamole sauce, I wouldn't have like it one bit. The chicken was quite spicy (even though it didn't say it was suppose to be spicy) & there wasn't enough romaine lettuce in my opinion. However, each order does come with a side of tortilla chips & the burritos are definitely big enough to feed two!"}]}

{'name': 'Surf Dog', 'address': 'The Bluffs Parking Lot', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Hot Dogs', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2017-02-25 05:41:32', 'review_text': 'He treated me with such respect when stopping for a bite on my cycling and knew just what would be the best for me. So missed before I could turn you onto other fellow friend cyclists.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-02-28 20:34:48', 'review_text': "So sorry to hear Bill passed away. He was the nicest man, kind and thoughtful. We'll miss him"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-02-15 05:17:27', 'review_text': "Bye Bye Bill.... 

A hotdog stand now in heaven to quench the love that is always needed everywhere.  I really will miss you on that corner with your wit and caring banter. 

past review.... AN OASIS ....  Don't drive by without stopping...  Great hotdogs, views, customers are a hoot and Bill has a viable suggestion for any challenge. I met him as he was lecturing in a business class.  An oasis....  Seal Rookery down the trail...  Very COOL"}]}

{'name': "Pollofino's", 'address': '6831 Hollister Ave', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': None, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-03-29 15:50:33', 'review_text': 'Pretty overpriced for a small portion of average quality food.




-'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-02-11 16:16:53', 'review_text': "3 stars
It's not that bad as a resturaunt the service is fine and the food comes at a good speed and you can maybe hear a sizzle in the kitchen. the quesadillas are good and so are the burritos but the tomatoes really overpower the other flavors which I don't like and the guacamole is sad and bland, If you buy a container of guacamole its not worth it because it is overpriced for the size and it tastes very sad and bland like it was just mourning a dead relative. Overall not bad I guess may eat there again. Don't judge the resturaunt completely off my rating because it is very good there is just some things I dont like."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-12-27 04:08:53', 'review_text': 'Simply the best most delicious chicken and tri tip in town. Great prices too & dependable quality. The char chicken burrito deluxe is my staple although the No. 1 Combo and Fajitas are also favorites. You cannot go wrong here. This is the first place I bring my guests to impress. All smiles.'}]}

{'name': 'August Ridge Vineyards', 'address': '5 E Figueroa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Wineries, Arts & Entertainment, Wine Tasting Room, Wine Bars, Nightlife, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '12:0-19:0', 'Thursday': '12:0-19:0', 'Friday': '12:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-20:0', 'Sunday': '12:0-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-08-10 02:22:21', 'review_text': 'My wife and I eloped last fall and stopped in for an impromptu wine tasting during that weekend. It was the best tasting experience we have ever had! The service was unparalleled and the wine was absolutely delicious. (The gentleman that helped us was wearing a super cool hummingbird shirt.... Thanks for the tasting!)

I would highly recommend that if you ever find yourself in SB, you make it a point to stop by! I know we will when we make it back! Thanks for giving us one of our favorite memories of the weekend!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-07-18 00:10:26', 'review_text': 'Wow, such a fan! Came here for special event that included a tasting. I really love the Italian varietals offered which is kind of rare for this area since most of the wineries produce Rhône varietals. The winemaker himself shared details about the production of the wine which made it really interactive. I really like whites but they are all really enjoyable. My favorite white was the Pinot Grigio. 

Even as a local of four years, I had never visited any of the businesses in Arcada Plaza. I found out that many businesses there have a deal where they waive the corkage fee if you bring in a bottle from August Ridge, super great info! I would highly recommend this tasting room to friends who want to try out different varietals!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-06-13 02:50:49', 'review_text': 'Looking forward to coming here soon'}]}

{'name': 'Trattoria Vittoria', 'address': '30 E Victoria St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Italian, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '17:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-21:0', 'Friday': '17:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '17:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '17:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': None, 'street': True, 'lot': False, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': None, 'divey': False, 'intimate': None, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': None, 'casual': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 04:55:39', 'review_text': "Great italian food. came here on a whim and thorough enjoyed it. will return next time i'm visiting santa barbara."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-11 08:50:25', 'review_text': "Their homemade pasta dishes, lasagna, tortellini and ravioli with a heavenly tomato sauce was definitely one of the most delicious dishes I've tried (and then I've been to Italy). The servers where so funny and genuine, too. We'll be back in SB when we get the chance!"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-08 17:23:35', 'review_text': 'We had an early dinner here. It filled up fast so if you can make reservations you should. 

We had an awesome dinner. Atmosphere was perfect.  Wine was delicious and the service was great. 

Next time I will come early and have a drink at the bar. Looked like a fun crowd. Enjoy!'}]}

{'name': 'Pacific Crêpes', 'address': '705 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Wine Bars, Restaurants, Gluten-Free, French, Bars, Nightlife, Creperies', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-15:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-15:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-15:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-15:0', 'Friday': '10:0-15:0', 'Saturday': '9:0-15:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-15:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-09-21 13:12:45', 'review_text': 'All their salads are good but my daughter and I loved the Monaco and Celtic salad the best,  and they also have a lot of choices for crepes. Great food, good customer service and reasonable price...I will definitely recommend this place! Keep it up, Pacific Crepes!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-02-17 21:29:46', 'review_text': "We will miss Pacific Crêpes. They were the real thing. The owners were from Brittany, France. When the mother worked there she ONLY spoke French, even if the customers couldn't. I still don't know how much English she could speak. They hosted our French conversation group for many years (we now meet Wednesdays at Arnoldi's; if you speak a little français come join us). Au revoir, PC!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-11-26 06:51:57', 'review_text': 'Delicious and unique french cafe.  Wonderful service.  Amazing coffee too.  Try coffee Mocca.

Enjoy!

We will be back!'}]}

{'name': 'On the Side', 'address': '6521 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (Traditional), Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2010-08-04 21:32:49', 'review_text': "Meh.

